    LLM: 'Game: Droggn. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Droggn is a rare Tyrolean trick-taking game from the Stubai Valley, historically played with a unique 66-card Tarock deck. It is a descendant of the Tarock L'Hombre family, making it distinct from more common Austrian variants like KÃ¶nigrufen. Known for its specific Tyrolean dialect terminology and the tactical use of the 'Fox' card, the game survived in the alpine villages of Fulpmes and Telfes as a testament to localized card-playing traditions.",
    objective: 'As declarer, take at least 37 card points (half of 74) in tricks to win the contract.',
    gameplay: '1. Bidding: Players compete for the contract.\n2. Talon Exchange: Declarer can swap cards with the blind.\n3. Trick Play: High and low Pip rankings exist. Tarocks always win. Follow suit required; Trumping required if void.',
